# Running tests

Before running any test commands in this project (e.g. `npm test`, `npm run mocha`, `npm run test:unit`), make sure the Node version from `.nvmrc` is active:

```bash
nvm use
```

This ensures the Node version from `.nvmrc` is active. Skipping it can cause SyntaxError or other version-related failures.

If the pinned version is already installed directly and `nvm` is not available, verifying the active runtime against `.nvmrc` is sufficient — do not abort just because `nvm` is missing:

```bash
test "v$(cat .nvmrc)" = "$(node -v)"
```
